  "user_request_original": "Design a 22-layer planar multilayer infrared filter coating on CaF2 (Daimon-20) substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees. Use alternating ZnS and MgF2 layers starting with ZnS as layer 1. Optimize individual layer thicknesses with bounds 50-1000 nm per layer. Target high transmittance in two passbands: 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm. Target low transmittance in two stopbands: 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Use coherent thin-film matrix method solver. Evaluate unpolarized light at normal incidence. Maximum 24 layers constraint satisfied with 22 layers. No metal layers used. Materials ZnS and MgF2 are from the guaranteed material catalog. Substrate is CaF2 (Daimon-20).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 22-layer alternating ZnS/MgF2 infrared dielectric filter on a CaF2 substrate, optimizing all layer thicknesses between 50 and 1000 nm. Maximize average transmittance in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm bands while minimizing it in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm bands at normal unpolarized incidence using a coherent transfer-matrix solver.",
